From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: de33: latch the address first on any layer geometry change

0032 programs a new buffer address alone and waits one frame before the
size and pitch only when the source grows. A shrinking source has the same
problem: when labwc goes back from composition (1920x1080 XRGB, no scaler)
to direct scan-out of a 1280x720 client buffer scaled on the HDMI plane,
the rest of the frame read the old buffer with the new pitch and scaler, a
black/garbled flash each time a notification went away. Latch the address
first on any change of source size, on-screen size, pitch or format.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c	2026-10-09 22:34:57.148940146 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c	2026-10-09 22:34:57.190421859 +0200
@@ -220,9 +220,19 @@
 	if (!old_state->visible || !old_state->fb || !new_state->fb ||
 	    old_state->crtc != new_state->crtc)
 		return;
-	if (drm_rect_width(&new_state->src) <= drm_rect_width(&old_state->src) &&
-	    drm_rect_height(&new_state->src) <= drm_rect_height(&old_state->src) &&
-	    new_state->fb->pitches[0] <= old_state->fb->pitches[0])
+	/*
+	 * Any change of source size, on-screen size, pitch or format, not only
+	 * a growing source: a shrinking one (composited desktop -> scaled
+	 * client scan-out on HDMI, when a notification goes away) read the
+	 * old buffer with the new pitch and scaler for the rest of the frame,
+	 * a visible flash.
+	 */
+	if (drm_rect_width(&new_state->src) == drm_rect_width(&old_state->src) &&
+	    drm_rect_height(&new_state->src) == drm_rect_height(&old_state->src) &&
+	    drm_rect_width(&new_state->dst) == drm_rect_width(&old_state->dst) &&
+	    drm_rect_height(&new_state->dst) == drm_rect_height(&old_state->dst) &&
+	    new_state->fb->pitches[0] == old_state->fb->pitches[0] &&
+	    new_state->fb->format == old_state->fb->format)
 		return;
 	crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_new_crtc_state(state, new_state->crtc);
 	if (!crtc_state || !crtc_state->active ||
